00:00:25.546 --> 00:00:26.379
Oh my God.

00:00:27.302 --> 00:00:29.227
- I can never raise the price.

00:00:29.227 --> 00:00:30.491
- Oh my God.

00:00:30.491 --> 00:00:33.364
You win for best tattoo ever.

00:00:33.364 --> 00:00:34.321
Oh my God.

00:00:34.321 --> 00:00:35.268
That was amazing.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.380
(Margaret laughs)

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.685
Okay. So there's no segue

00:00:37.685 --> 00:00:40.294
but for summer, do you do anything?

00:00:40.294 --> 00:00:42.366
Did y'all ever do family
vacations growing up?

00:00:42.366 --> 00:00:45.949
- Well, I would go to
Hawaii with my family

00:00:47.674 --> 00:00:50.828
for, you know, just for summer and stuff.

00:00:50.828 --> 00:00:51.961
And so,

00:00:51.961 --> 00:00:54.558
but the thing is I travel so much

00:00:54.558 --> 00:00:58.296
for my work that now I
really love to stay home.

00:00:58.296 --> 00:00:59.129
- [Kelly] Staycation.

00:00:59.129 --> 00:01:00.626
- Staycation.

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:01.459
I have

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.033
a garden of carnivorous plants.

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.256
So plants that eat bugs.

00:01:08.256 --> 00:01:09.089
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:01:09.089 --> 00:01:10.638
- So I just watch 'em.

00:01:10.638 --> 00:01:11.871
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.176
It's so fun.

00:01:13.176 --> 00:01:14.244
- That is so messed up.

00:01:14.244 --> 00:01:15.077
- I love it.

00:01:15.077 --> 00:01:17.254
And then, you just have like

00:01:17.254 --> 00:01:18.427
such a busy life,

00:01:18.427 --> 00:01:20.561
so it's great to just be home

00:01:20.561 --> 00:01:21.547
and do nothing.

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:24.790
And then I have a bathtub
now in my backyard.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.310
- [Kelly] Yes. What?

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.059
- [Margaret] It's kind of
like an above-ground pool.

00:01:28.059 --> 00:01:29.392
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:01:29.392 --> 00:01:31.394
- See, there's like hot glue.

00:01:31.394 --> 00:01:33.239
I was putting up some things.

00:01:33.239 --> 00:01:34.600
I know it's so Bridgerton.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:35.677
- It's so good.

00:01:35.677 --> 00:01:36.773
- I'm living.

00:01:36.773 --> 00:01:38.622
I'm like, yeah, I fill
it up with the hose.

00:01:38.622 --> 00:01:39.721
- Yes.

00:01:39.721 --> 00:01:41.277
- No, it's really nice.

00:01:41.277 --> 00:01:44.860
And then I put like a
movie screen outside,

00:01:45.721 --> 00:01:48.100
so I have a couch so I can watch movies,

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.098
and so I watch scary movies.

00:01:50.098 --> 00:01:51.264
- Wait, what?

00:01:51.264 --> 00:01:52.679
At night?
- At night

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.727
And it's all kind of woods behind me

00:01:54.727 --> 00:01:56.245
and it's so scary.

00:01:56.245 --> 00:01:57.919
And it's so fun.

00:01:57.919 --> 00:01:58.877
(audience laughs)

00:01:58.877 --> 00:02:01.990
- You have a very weird
idea of what fun is to me.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:03.891
- Isn't that fun though?
- [Kelly] No.

00:02:03.891 --> 00:02:04.724
- You don't like scary movies?

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:07.148
- Nope. I don't like to be scared.

00:02:07.148 --> 00:02:08.843
- Oh see, I love scary movies

00:02:08.843 --> 00:02:11.191
because I'm always
thinking the worst thing

00:02:11.191 --> 00:02:12.242
is gonna happen to me.

00:02:12.242 --> 00:02:14.255
So when I watch scary movies, I can relax.

00:02:14.255 --> 00:02:15.088
- [Kelly] You're prepared.

00:02:15.088 --> 00:02:15.921
You're prepared.

00:02:15.921 --> 00:02:19.318
- Yeah, because I'm a
catastrophic thinker.

00:02:19.318 --> 00:02:21.214
I like to think, "Oh, the
worst is gonna happen."

00:02:21.214 --> 00:02:24.645
So it's almost like I
pre-feel the emotions.

00:02:24.645 --> 00:02:25.753
- Wait, I do that with certain things,

00:02:25.753 --> 00:02:26.812
especially when I was pregnant.

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:28.007
I literally, this sounds messed up,

00:02:28.007 --> 00:02:30.132
but I would go through like
the worst-case scenario.

00:02:30.132 --> 00:02:31.289
'Cause when I walked in there, I was like,

00:02:31.289 --> 00:02:32.122
"I just wanna be prepared

00:02:32.122 --> 00:02:33.805
if that is said to me" like what I need to

00:02:33.805 --> 00:02:35.638
I don't want it to be the first time

00:02:35.638 --> 00:02:36.623
that I'm thinking about it.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:37.456
- Rehearsing.

00:02:37.456 --> 00:02:38.289
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:02:38.289 --> 00:02:40.653
- Like you're rehearsing the feelings

00:02:40.653 --> 00:02:42.338
so that it won't be such a shock.

00:02:42.338 --> 00:02:43.171
- Yes.

00:02:43.171 --> 00:02:44.629
But I also think you
might be setting yourself

00:02:44.629 --> 00:02:46.212
up for a Dateline Special

00:02:46.212 --> 00:02:48.067
by going outside at nighttime

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.375
by the woods

00:02:49.375 --> 00:02:51.970
naked in a bathtub,
watching a scary movie.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:53.121
- I mean, but it's all my house.

00:02:53.121 --> 00:02:55.782
And I have dogs and really mean cats.

00:02:55.782 --> 00:02:56.615
- Oh you have dogs.

00:02:56.615 --> 00:02:57.711
See, and they'll alert you.

00:02:57.711 --> 00:02:58.544
That's true. Okay.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:02:59.880
- [Margaret] So, you
know, it's kind of like-

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.148
- Have your Bridgerton moment.

00:03:01.148 --> 00:03:02.061
- I have my animals.

00:03:02.061 --> 00:03:04.012
I have my carnivorous plants.

00:03:04.012 --> 00:03:05.080
I mean, I have, you know,

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.893
- My carnivorous plants. (laughing)

00:03:06.893 --> 00:03:09.564
- That seems like defense enough.

00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:10.696
- [Kelly] Yeah, I like it.

00:03:10.696 --> 00:03:12.077
Yeah, I like it.

00:03:12.077 --> 00:03:12.910
- Yeah.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:14.754
- So you're newly single.

00:03:14.754 --> 00:03:15.935
So I know what that's like.

00:03:15.935 --> 00:03:17.783
So do you like having the
place all to yourself?

00:03:17.783 --> 00:03:18.616
'Cause I enjoy it.

00:03:18.616 --> 00:03:19.715
- Yes, I love it so much.

00:03:19.715 --> 00:03:20.751
I love it

00:03:20.751 --> 00:03:21.709
so much.

00:03:21.709 --> 00:03:22.596
- Like your room.

00:03:22.596 --> 00:03:23.688
You're like, "This is my bed."

00:03:23.688 --> 00:03:26.392
- I sleep smack in the middle.

00:03:26.392 --> 00:03:28.233
- Yeah? I don't do that.

00:03:28.233 --> 00:03:29.352
- I sleep in the middle,

00:03:29.352 --> 00:03:31.532
and then I have all my animals around me.

00:03:31.532 --> 00:03:32.701
And it's great.

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:35.902
All you need is a really crazy
high-tech security system

00:03:35.902 --> 00:03:37.041
and then you're fine.

00:03:37.041 --> 00:03:37.874
- [Kelly] Exactly.

00:03:37.874 --> 00:03:39.503
- I feel like that's
all you need to be safe.

00:03:39.503 --> 00:03:40.336
- The dogs too.

00:03:40.336 --> 00:03:41.169
- And dogs.

00:03:41.169 --> 00:03:44.001
But you think that you feel
you need another person

00:03:44.001 --> 00:03:45.256
to keep you safe

00:03:45.256 --> 00:03:46.839
but actually, no.

00:03:46.839 --> 00:03:48.656
They're actually the dangerous one.

00:03:48.656 --> 00:03:50.996
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:53.967
It's coming from inside the house.

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:56.967
(audience applauds)

00:03:58.164 --> 00:04:00.706
- It's coming from inside.

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:01.539
- You know?

00:04:01.539 --> 00:04:02.372
- Yeah.

00:04:02.372 --> 00:04:03.205
- But isn't it great?

00:04:03.205 --> 00:04:04.142
Don't you feel so good?

00:04:04.142 --> 00:04:05.725
- You are so funny.

00:04:06.639 --> 00:04:07.472
No, I do.

00:04:07.472 --> 00:04:10.498
And I used to be terrified by myself,

00:04:10.498 --> 00:04:12.345
but now I think 'cause I have two littles

00:04:12.345 --> 00:04:13.286
in my house with me,

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.486
then I'm the mama bear.

00:04:14.486 --> 00:04:15.641
So I don't get like that.

00:04:15.641 --> 00:04:17.666
I have dogs and a
security system, and yeah.

00:04:17.666 --> 00:04:19.466
- But you have to be there

00:04:19.466 --> 00:04:21.053
and not be afraid for them.

00:04:21.053 --> 00:04:21.886
- Yeah.

00:04:21.886 --> 00:04:22.922
You have to act like you're

00:04:22.922 --> 00:04:23.755
Like the power went out the other day

00:04:23.755 --> 00:04:25.809
and my kid freaked out,

00:04:25.809 --> 00:04:27.807
and I was trying to make it all fun.

00:04:27.807 --> 00:04:29.267
Like da, da, da, and still he's like

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:30.757
my kid, he got so scarred, y'all.

00:04:30.757 --> 00:04:32.073
He walks around my house,

00:04:32.073 --> 00:04:33.366
and he turns off the lights everywhere,

00:04:33.366 --> 00:04:34.436
which I'm like, "That's good."

00:04:34.436 --> 00:04:35.432
Like energy efficient.

00:04:35.432 --> 00:04:36.265
- Yeah.

00:04:36.265 --> 00:04:37.098
- But he's terrified.

00:04:37.098 --> 00:04:38.300
He's like, "We can't use the lights up,

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.470
'cause they might all go out"

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:40.524
and he was like terrified.

00:04:40.524 --> 00:04:41.540
So, yeah.
- [Margaret] Oh.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:42.706
- I know. That's actually really sad.

00:04:42.706 --> 00:04:44.236
I don't know why I said that.

00:04:44.236 --> 00:04:45.069
(audience laughs)

00:04:45.069 --> 00:04:46.587
But you like to get out sometimes though

00:04:46.587 --> 00:04:47.995
'cause I heard that Harrison Ford,

00:04:47.995 --> 00:04:49.947
did he spill wine all over you once?

00:04:49.947 --> 00:04:50.780
- Well, yeah.

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:51.613
I was at a party.
- [Kelly] It's a good story.

00:04:51.613 --> 00:04:52.796
- This is years ago

00:04:52.796 --> 00:04:53.823
at Carrie Fisher's house.

00:04:53.823 --> 00:04:55.179
Carrie Fisher and Penny
Marshall used to do

00:04:55.179 --> 00:04:56.903
a joint birthday party every year.

00:04:56.903 --> 00:05:00.347
So I went and Harrison Ford was there.

00:05:00.347 --> 00:05:01.901
Everybody there was a celebrity.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.942
And it was so weird.

00:05:03.942 --> 00:05:05.260
- I've never been to that party.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:07.102
- It was such a strange,

00:05:07.102 --> 00:05:08.981
it was like being in Madame Tussauds

00:05:08.981 --> 00:05:10.992
because they were all famous.

00:05:10.992 --> 00:05:12.471
And I was just like walking in

00:05:12.471 --> 00:05:15.553
and then Harrison Ford was walking through

00:05:15.553 --> 00:05:18.460
with like three glasses of red wine

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.727
in little plastic cups, like

00:05:20.727 --> 00:05:22.786
and I mean, he should
be able to carry them

00:05:22.786 --> 00:05:24.626
'cause he's Indiana Jones and Han Solo,

00:05:24.626 --> 00:05:27.338
so he should be able to
carry three glasses of wine.

00:05:27.338 --> 00:05:29.214
- What a let down.

00:05:29.214 --> 00:05:32.172
- But he walked up and he goes, "Whoa."

00:05:32.172 --> 00:05:33.325
And he fell

00:05:33.325 --> 00:05:36.188
and threw all of the
wine on me, like all on.

00:05:36.188 --> 00:05:38.044
But it was him.

00:05:38.044 --> 00:05:39.329
(audience laughs)

00:05:39.329 --> 00:05:40.899
- You were like, "Fine."

00:05:40.899 --> 00:05:42.089
- I was like, "It's fine."

00:05:42.089 --> 00:05:44.699
I mean, I was kind of really excited.

00:05:44.699 --> 00:05:46.153
I was really starstruck.

00:05:46.153 --> 00:05:47.371
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:47.371 --> 00:05:48.601
I was really excited.

00:05:48.601 --> 00:05:49.623
- Was he so embarrassed?

00:05:49.623 --> 00:05:50.456
- He was so embarrassed.

00:05:50.456 --> 00:05:52.122
And he was like, he grabbed a napkin

00:05:52.122 --> 00:05:53.521
but it was on my front

00:05:53.521 --> 00:05:55.229
and he was like, "Oh, oh, oh."

00:05:55.229 --> 00:05:57.364
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:57.364 --> 00:05:59.030
- Can't pat it down.
- Didn't know what to do.

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:01.789
And it was just the most adorable thing.

00:06:01.789 --> 00:06:03.005
It was really, really sweet.

00:06:03.005 --> 00:06:05.159
- I love that you're like,
"Han Solo and Indiana Jones.

00:06:05.159 --> 00:06:06.129
What an epic fail."

00:06:06.129 --> 00:06:08.503
- He could've just whipped
off the stain maybe.

00:06:08.503 --> 00:06:09.719
But I don't know.

00:06:09.719 --> 00:06:11.380
He's just very,

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:14.762
it was one of my favorite
celebrity moments.

00:06:14.762 --> 00:06:15.912
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:06:15.912 --> 00:06:16.745
- That was exciting.

00:06:16.745 --> 00:06:18.068
- Yeah. That's cool.

00:06:18.068 --> 00:06:19.867
Well, speaking of parties

00:06:19.867 --> 00:06:21.468
your new movie is called "Fire Island."

00:06:21.468 --> 00:06:22.301
- [Margaret] Yes.

00:06:22.301 --> 00:06:24.574
- Which is known for
summer parties, right?

00:06:24.574 --> 00:06:26.299
- Well, it's a

00:06:26.299 --> 00:06:28.322
beautiful place.

00:06:28.322 --> 00:06:31.764
It's a very gay summer romantic location.

00:06:31.764 --> 00:06:33.847
And the movie is written
by Joel Kim Booster.

00:06:33.847 --> 00:06:34.680
He stars in it.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:36.895
He's an incredible, incredible comedian,

00:06:36.895 --> 00:06:38.618
incredible writer, incredible actor

00:06:38.618 --> 00:06:39.973
and Bowen Yang stars in it,

00:06:39.973 --> 00:06:42.514
and Matt Rogers, who's
a huge fan of yours.

00:06:42.514 --> 00:06:43.706
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:06:43.706 --> 00:06:44.780
I like him already.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:47.565
- And we talked about you
a lot actually on the set.

00:06:47.565 --> 00:06:48.754
And we had a great time talking

00:06:48.754 --> 00:06:51.871
about you, and he had
actually come with Joel

00:06:51.871 --> 00:06:52.871
to this show

00:06:54.619 --> 00:06:55.599
and stayed backstage

00:06:55.599 --> 00:06:57.168
and cried in the dressing room

00:06:57.168 --> 00:06:59.729
'cause he loves you so much.

00:06:59.729 --> 00:07:01.479
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.
- But he was so nervous.

00:07:01.479 --> 00:07:03.380
Didn't wanna rock the boat.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:05.771
- What? I'm like the most friendly person.

00:07:05.771 --> 00:07:06.604
- I know.

00:07:06.604 --> 00:07:09.326
I wish he could be here, but he loves you.

00:07:09.326 --> 00:07:10.626
- [Kelly] Oh. Well next time.

00:07:10.626 --> 00:07:12.496
- Yes.
- Okay. We need a quick break.

00:07:12.496 --> 00:07:14.475
You can see Margaret in
"The Flight Attendant",

00:07:14.475 --> 00:07:16.246
which I'm so excited about on HBO Max.

00:07:16.246 --> 00:07:19.641
And watch out for "Fire Island"
premiering tomorrow on Hulu.

